<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  ГЛАВНАЯ. The screen the app opens on.
  ============================================================================

  READ THIS BEFORE CHANGING THE SHAPE OF THIS FILE.

  `docs/design2026/13-start-screen.md` carries an OWNER OVERRULE dated 2026-07-26:
  its SCOPE is void and only its VISUAL language survives. A wave built this screen
  "from nothing" out of that document, replaced the inline server list and the
  subscription card with two navigation rows, and replaced the connect object -
  concentric rings, the running animation, the country flag - with a bare disc. The
  owner compared the two builds and rejected it:

      «как выглядела главная по функционалу такая и должна остаться»
      «и дизайн кнопки другой совсем, хотя был другой раньше и анимация была»
      «все должно быть вернуто с пилюлей и инфой о подписке под кнопкой»

  So: **Главная is a RESTYLE.** Same controls, same capabilities, same information,
  same motion, drawn on the component layer with tokens and the type ramp.

  WHAT IS ON THIS SCREEN, top to bottom:

      [ 56 ] the account row, FIRST                   layout_home_account.xml
      [ 48 ] the add action, alone on its line, right
      [ 56 ] the «Привязать Telegram» banner, in one state only
      [  1 ] hairline, alpha 0 until the content scrolls
      [ 48 ] the status strip, only when a condition applies
      [ 24 ]
      [224 ] the connect object: three concentric rings, one disc, one glyph
      [ 16 ]
      [ 24 ] the ledger: ↑ 1,0 KB/s   00:11:52   ↓ 1,2 KB/s   - one line, no captions
      [ 22 ] the flag and the server, ONE centred line in the accent, bold
      [ 24 ]
      [  * ] the subscription card, one page per subscription
      [  * ] the server list, inline - this is the ONLY place a server is picked
      [ 24 ]

  THE ACCOUNT ROW IS AT THE TOP AND THE LEDGER HAS NO CAPTIONS, and both are the owner
  measuring this build against the one he approved, on 2026-08-03:

      «плюсик лучше сделать ниже аккаунта»          - the add action held the first band
      «↑ 1,0 KB/s  00:11:52  ↓ 1,2 KB/s»            - one line, arrows, no labels
      «No «Отключено» word above it, and no grey circular flag tile»

  Do not put the stacked «Отдача, Мбит/с» / «Время сессии» / «Приём, Мбит/с» captions
  back, and do not put a status word above the server line. Read the notes at each.

  or, when there is not one server to connect to, the gate block in place of the
  card and the list (layout_home_empty.xml). Never both.

  THE RINGS ARE BACK AND THEY ARE NOT DECORATION. The connect object's own three
  concentric rings are its state channel - one hue at three opacities, a geometry
  that never changes size - and they are the reason the owner recognised the screen.
  They come back. The halo glow does not.

  THE BLUE GROUND IS THE OWNER'S, AND THIS ROOT MUST STAY TRANSPARENT.
  The shell (`activity_main.xml`, `home_root`) paints `@drawable/bg_home_gradient` -
  the brand's blue ground, with a light and a `drawable-night` twin - behind every
  tab. Настройки and Аккаунт let it through; this file used to paint
  `?android:attr/colorBackground` over it, an opaque flat token that covered the
  gradient in BOTH themes. That is exactly what the owner reported on 2026-08-02:
  «синего фона нет на светлой и темной версии на главной». The blue was never
  removed from the tokens - it was hidden by one attribute on one view.
  So: `@android:color/transparent`. The screen's ground is the shell's gradient, and
  the mono overlay's neutral variant reaches it through
  `MainActivity.applyThemeDecorations`. Do not reintroduce an opaque fill here.

  ZERO RAW VALUES. No dp, no sp, no hex, no fontFamily, no textSize anywhere in
  this file - every number is a token and every text element carries only a
  textAppearance.

  clipChildren / clipToPadding are false the whole way down because the confirm
  ring scales past its own frame.
-->
<androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/home_tab_root"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="@android:color/transparent"
    android:clipChildren="false"
    android:clipToPadding="false"
    android:fillViewport="true"
    android:scrollbars="none">

    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/home_content"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:clipChildren="false"
        android:orientation="vertical"
        android:paddingBottom="@dimen/space_24">

        <!-- THE ACCOUNT ROW IS THE FIRST THING ON THE SCREEN, and that is an owner
             instruction, not a preference: «сверху где отображается на главной аккаунт
             типа управление аккаунтом, оно НЕ В САМОМ ВЕРХУ, выше плюсик и это лишнее
             пространство занимает, плюсик лучше сделать НИЖЕ аккаунта». The add action
             used to hold a 48dp band above it, holding nothing else since the ledger
             moved under the connect object, so the screen opened on an empty strip.

             Rows bleed to the screen edge so their press feedback does; each row
             carries the 16dp gutter itself, from @style/Widget.Departament.Row. -->
        <include
            android:id="@+id/layout_home_account"
            layout="@layout/layout_home_account" />

        <!--
          THE ADD ACTION, UNDER THE ACCOUNT ROW. Adding a subscription is the one thing
          this screen owns that is not the connection, so it sits alone at the right and
          opens the SAME menu every other add entry point does. 48dp box, 24dp glyph:
          the touch-target floor with no fixed height on its row.

          THE LEDGER USED TO SHARE ITS LINE, AND IT DOES NOT ANY MORE. отдача · время
          сессии · приём now sit UNDER the connect object — «скорость почему-то вверху,
          хотя должны быть под кнопкой» — which is also where the desktop carries them
          (ConnectHeroView.axaml, StatsRow: «Стата-строка ПОД щитом, НАД именем
          сервера»). See @id/numeric_strip.
        -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/home_top_row"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:baselineAligned="false"
            android:gravity="center_vertical|end"
            android:orientation="horizontal"
            android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
            android:paddingEnd="@dimen/space_4">

            <ImageView
                android:id="@+id/btn_home_add"
                android:layout_width="@dimen/view_height_dp48"
                android:layout_height="@dimen/view_height_dp48"
                android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackgroundBorderless"
                android:clickable="true"
                android:contentDescription="@string/home_add_subscription"
                android:focusable="true"
                android:padding="@dimen/space_12"
                android:scaleType="fitCenter"
                app:srcCompat="@drawable/ic_add_24dp"
                app:tint="?attr/colorOnSurface" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <!--
          THE «ПРИВЯЗАТЬ TELEGRAM» BANNER, restored from 5e8cd54 (owner rule,
          2026-08-02: an element that was on screen and is now gone is a
          regression).

          It exists for exactly one state, and nothing else on this screen covers
          it: a user who PASTED a departament подписка and has never signed in. He
          has servers, so there is no gate block at all; and the gate's own
          «Привязать Telegram» secondary belongs to the signed-in-with-no-подписка
          shape, so it never reaches him.

          DISMISSIBLE, and the dismissal is remembered: this is an offer, not an
          error, and an offer that returns on every launch is nagging. The ✕ is a
          40dp target beside a row that is itself the primary action, which is the
          one place two targets on one line are sanctioned (a banner is not a row).
        -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/cta_link_telegram"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
            android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
            android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter"
            android:background="@drawable/bg_server_card"
            android:baselineAligned="false"
            android:clickable="true"
            android:focusable="true"
            android:gravity="center_vertical"
            android:minHeight="@dimen/row_min_height"
            android:orientation="horizontal"
            android:paddingStart="@dimen/space_12"
            android:paddingTop="@dimen/space_8"
            android:paddingEnd="@dimen/space_4"
            android:paddingBottom="@dimen/space_8"
            android:stateListAnimator="@anim/press_scale"
            android:visibility="gone"
            tools:visibility="visible">

            <ImageView
                android:layout_width="@dimen/tile_glyph"
                android:layout_height="@dimen/tile_glyph"
                android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                android:src="@drawable/ic_telegram_24dp" />

            <TextView
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_12"
                android:layout_weight="1"
                android:text="@string/auth_link_telegram_cta"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle" />

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/btn_cta_dismiss"
                android:layout_width="@dimen/view_height_dp48"
                android:layout_height="@dimen/view_height_dp48"
                android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackgroundBorderless"
                android:clickable="true"
                android:contentDescription="@string/auth_link_telegram_cta_dismiss"
                android:focusable="true"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:text="✕"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
                android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- The ONLY scroll-linked change on this screen: no colour step, no
             elevation, no shadow, no collapsing title. -->
        <View
            android:id="@+id/header_hairline"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/stroke_hairline"
            android:alpha="0"
            android:background="?attr/colorOutlineVariant"
            android:importantForAccessibility="no" />

        <!-- The shared status-strip component in its INLINE placement: a persistent
             CONDITION, no auto-dismiss. Its hairline is hidden and its bar is
             clipped to @dimen/radius_control from HomeFragment, which is the only
             difference from the shell's docked placement of the same file. -->
        <include
            android:id="@+id/layout_status_strip"
            layout="@layout/view_status_strip"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
            android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_12"
            android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter" />

        <Space
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/space_24" />

        <!--
          THE CONNECT OBJECT. THREE CONCENTRIC RINGS, ONE DISC, ONE GLYPH.

          The rings are the reason the owner recognised the screen, and the reason he
          did not recognise the build that dropped them. They are not decoration
          around the object - they ARE the object's state channel: one colour at
          three rising opacities, outermost faintest, so the whole assembly reads
          idle grey, negotiating amber-blue, connected accent, failed red, on a
          geometry that never changes size.

          THE WHOLE ASSEMBLY IS THE CONTROL. connect_frame is 176 + 24 either side =
          224dp of touch target and @anim/press_scale scales rings, disc and shield
          together, because they are one object. The ring colours, the ripple and the
          2dp focus ring are built in HomeFragment from theme attributes - a drawable
          file cannot carry a runtime-tinted stroke without the raw hex the old
          bg_connect_ring.xml shipped, and two of that file's six hex literals
          measured 2.33:1 and 1.29:1 against the ground.

          The banned parts of the old hero did NOT come back with the rings: there is
          no accent glow bleeding out behind the shield and no page gradient under
          the screen. The breathing that used to live on that glow lives on the rings
          now, where it is the object telling you it is negotiating.

          IT IS ALIVE AT REST TOO, AND THE PRESS GOES THREE LAYERS DEEP. The owner:
          «при нажатии на кнопку практически нет никакой анимации, только пульсация, а
          на ПК по другому анимация сделана». Both halves of that are the desktop's, and
          both are here now:

            - the AMBIENT layer (HomeFragment.startAmbient) - a six-second breath on the
              two outer rings and a wave leaving the disc (@id/connect_ring_ambient),
              running at rest AND while connected, out of phase so the pair reads as
              alive rather than as a metronome. It stands down for the negotiating
              breath, under reduced motion, and while the app is in the background.
              ConnectHeroView.axaml: AmbientRing.breathe-idle/-live +
              AmbientSonar.rest-idle/-live.
            - the PARALLAX PRESS - @anim/press_scale 0.97 on this frame, @anim/press_dip
              0.97 again on the disc, and once more on the glyph, composing to the
              desktop's own 0.94 disc and 0.91 glyph. Plus the scrim already here.
        -->
        <FrameLayout
            android:id="@+id/connect_frame"
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_gravity="center_horizontal"
            android:clickable="true"
            android:clipChildren="false"
            android:clipToPadding="false"
            android:focusable="true"
            android:padding="@dimen/space_24"
            android:stateListAnimator="@anim/press_scale"
            tools:ignore="ContentDescription">

            <!-- Rings 3 and 2 of 3 are two layers of THIS view's background, inset
                 12dp apart, because a child of a padded FrameLayout can never be
                 wider than the padded box and the outer rings have to be. Ring 1 is
                 the disc's own. All three are built in HomeFragment.

                 The disc. Its fill and its own ring - the innermost and brightest of
                 the three - are built there too. -->
            <!--
              THE AMBIENT WAVE, and it is the layer this object was missing.

              FIRST child of the frame, so it lies UNDER the disc and everything the disc
              holds, and it is not hit-testable — the tap belongs to the frame. It starts
              at the disc's own 176dp (match_parent inside the frame's 24dp padding) and
              travels out through the two outer rings the frame's background draws.
              HomeFragment loops it slowly at rest and, a little brighter and faster,
              while connected: the desktop's «живой» layer (ConnectHeroView.axaml,
              AmbientSonar.rest-idle / rest-live). Without it the object was a still
              picture except during the 850ms negotiating breath, which is precisely the
              complaint — «практически нет никакой анимации, только пульсация».
            -->
            <View
                android:id="@+id/connect_ring_ambient"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_gravity="center"
                android:alpha="0"
                android:importantForAccessibility="no" />

            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/connect_disc"
                android:layout_width="@dimen/connect_disc"
                android:layout_height="@dimen/connect_disc"
                android:layout_gravity="center"
                android:clipChildren="false"
                android:duplicateParentState="true"
                android:stateListAnimator="@anim/press_dip">

                <!-- PRESS DEPTH. The disc darkens into the press — the desktop's
                     «колодец» (ConnectHeroView.axaml PressScrim, P1-2) — under the
                     shield, which draws over it and stays solid. It duplicates the
                     frame's pressed state through the disc, so @anim/press_scrim runs
                     in unison with @anim/press_scale on the frame; the object now has
                     the depth as well as the scale. Not hit-testable: the tap belongs
                     to the frame. -->
                <View
                    android:id="@+id/connect_press_scrim"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:alpha="0"
                    android:background="@drawable/bg_connect_press_scrim"
                    android:duplicateParentState="true"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    android:stateListAnimator="@anim/press_scrim" />

                <!-- THE CONFIRM PAYOFF: two rings and never three, emitted at the
                     instant the tunnel confirms and by no other event in the product.
                     The lead ring goes first; the echo follows it a beat later, dimmer
                     and travelling slightly less far, which is what makes the moment
                     read as locked rather than as a blip. Neither loops. This mirrors
                     the desktop's Sonar.pulsing + Sonar.pulsing-echo pair, whose own
                     note is «максимум ДВА кольца, не радар». -->
                <View
                    android:id="@+id/connect_ring_pulse_echo"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    android:visibility="invisible" />

                <View
                    android:id="@+id/connect_ring_pulse"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    android:visibility="invisible" />

                <!-- The negotiating sweep. indicatorSize == the disc, so the arc
                     travels the disc's own ring instead of orbiting outside it, at
                     that ring's stroke width; the static ring underneath IS the
                     track. It runs while the core is negotiating and while a
                     subscription is being fetched - the two states this screen has
                     ever spun it for. -->
                <com.google.android.material.progressindicator.CircularProgressIndicator
                    android:id="@+id/connect_sweep"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    android:indeterminate="true"
                    android:visibility="gone"
                    app:hideAnimationBehavior="inward"
                    app:indeterminateAnimationType="disjoint"
                    app:indicatorColor="?attr/colorPrimary"
                    app:indicatorSize="@dimen/connect_disc"
                    app:showAnimationBehavior="inward"
                    app:trackColor="@android:color/transparent"
                    app:trackCornerRadius="@dimen/stroke_emphasis"
                    app:trackThickness="@dimen/stroke_ring" />

                <!-- Two shields, crossfaded. Never tint-animated: the filled shield
                     is accent from frame zero and only its alpha moves.

                     THE GLYPH SINKS DEEPER THAN THE DISC. @anim/press_dip runs on both
                     shields as well as on the disc, so the press composes frame 0.97 ->
                     disc 0.97 -> glyph 0.97 and the glyph is pressed INTO the disc
                     rather than carried by it. That is the desktop's parallax dip
                     (ConnectHeroView.axaml.cs, «глиф вдавливается в диск чуть глубже
                     самого диска») and its figures land within a thousandth of ours.
                     duplicateParentState is what feeds them the frame's pressed state
                     through the disc. -->
                <ImageView
                    android:id="@+id/shield_outline"
                    android:layout_width="@dimen/shield_glyph"
                    android:layout_height="@dimen/shield_glyph"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:duplicateParentState="true"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    android:stateListAnimator="@anim/press_dip"
                    app:srcCompat="@drawable/ic_shield_outline"
                    app:tint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

                <ImageView
                    android:id="@+id/shield_filled"
                    android:layout_width="@dimen/shield_glyph"
                    android:layout_height="@dimen/shield_glyph"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:alpha="0"
                    android:duplicateParentState="true"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    android:stateListAnimator="@anim/press_dip"
                    app:srcCompat="@drawable/ic_shield_filled"
                    app:tint="?attr/colorPrimary" />
            </FrameLayout>
        </FrameLayout>

        <Space
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/space_16" />

        <!--
          THE STATUS LINE, AND IT IS TWO LINES AND NEVER THREE: the ledger, then the
          server. This and an empty state are the only centred text in the product.

          THE STATUS WORD ABOVE THE SERVER IS GONE. The owner measured this build
          against the one he approved and reported the difference: «No «Отключено»
          word above it, and no grey circular flag tile». Nothing is lost with it —
          the word only ever repeated what the object beside it was already saying in
          colour (grey idle, accent connected, red failed), and the ONE line below the
          ledger now carries the server when there is one and the state word when
          there is not, which is what the reference build did. See paintStatusLine.
        -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/status_line"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"
            android:gravity="center_horizontal"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
            android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter">

            <!--
              THE LEDGER: ↑ отдача · время сессии · ↓ приём, ONE COMPACT LINE with no
              captions under it, UNDER the connect object and ABOVE the server. That is
              the reference build, described by the owner to the character — «↑ 1,0 KB/s
              00:11:52 ↓ 1,2 KB/s», blue arrows, tabular figures, the timer in the
              middle — and the stacked «Отдача, Мбит/с» / «Время сессии» / «Приём,
              Мбит/с» captions this build grew are what he rejected. It is also the
              desktop's order (ConnectHeroView.axaml StatsRow, «ПОД щитом, НАД именем
              сервера»).

              THE ARROW IS THE LABEL. It costs one accent glyph instead of a two-word
              caption, it needs no translation, and it is what the anchor build drew.
              The unit rides WITH the value (0 KB/s -> 1,2 MB/s), because that is what
              @string/speed_zero and Long.toSpeedString have always produced and it is
              what the owner's screenshot shows; the caption that used to own the unit
              no longer exists to hold it.

              THE RESERVE IS THE WHOLE POINT: android:minEms reserves N em, and an em
              IS the text size, so the reserve scales with the type at every font scale
              without a single sp literal. A value going 9,9 -> 10,1 moves nothing, and
              neither does 00:09:59 -> 00:10:00.

              The strip is on screen at rest, reading zeroes, exactly as it was: this
              is the screen's ledger, not a reward for connecting, and a row that
              vanishes when idle is a row the user cannot find. HomeFragment lands the
              figures on it while a tunnel is up and returns them to zero when it goes.
            -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/numeric_strip"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
                android:baselineAligned="false"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:orientation="horizontal">

                <LinearLayout
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:baselineAligned="true"
                    android:gravity="center"
                    android:orientation="horizontal">

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/tv_up_arrow"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/space_4"
                        android:contentDescription="@string/home_strip_up_label"
                        android:text="@string/home_strip_up_arrow"
                        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
                        android:textColor="?attr/colorPrimary" />

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/tv_up"
                        style="@style/TextAppearance.App.Numeric"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:maxLines="1"
                        android:minEms="4"
                        android:text="@string/home_speed_zero"
                        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
                        tools:text="1,0 KB/s" />
                </LinearLayout>

                <!-- The session clock. Dead centre, because "how long have I been
                     protected" is a different question from "how fast is it". -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/tv_uptime"
                    style="@style/TextAppearance.App.Numeric"
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:gravity="center"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:text="@string/home_uptime_zero"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Title"
                    tools:text="00:11:52" />

                <LinearLayout
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:baselineAligned="true"
                    android:gravity="center"
                    android:orientation="horizontal">

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/tv_down_arrow"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/space_4"
                        android:contentDescription="@string/home_strip_down_label"
                        android:text="@string/home_strip_down_arrow"
                        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
                        android:textColor="?attr/colorPrimary" />

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/tv_down"
                        style="@style/TextAppearance.App.Numeric"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:maxLines="1"
                        android:minEms="4"
                        android:text="@string/home_speed_zero"
                        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
                        tools:text="1,2 KB/s" />
                </LinearLayout>
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- WHAT IT RUNS THROUGH: the flag and the server, ONE centred line under
                 the ledger, in the accent and bold. This is the second of the three
                 questions this screen answers, and in the reference build it is the
                 only text under the object.

                 THE FLAG IS A BARE GLYPH. It used to sit in a grey circular tile
                 (@drawable/bg_flag_tile) and the owner named that as a difference from
                 what he had: a tile is a LIST affordance — it gives the rows below a
                 common leading edge — and there is no column to align to here, so all
                 it did was hang a grey disc off the middle of a centred line.

                 ALWAYS VISIBLE, and that is what keeps the block below it still: the
                 line resolves to a server, a state word or an instruction in every
                 state there is, so it never has to be emptied and nothing under it can
                 move. It starts INVISIBLE only for the frames before the first render.
                 -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/server_identity"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_12"
                android:baselineAligned="true"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:minHeight="@dimen/tile_glyph"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:visibility="invisible"
                tools:visibility="visible">

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/tv_server_flag"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/space_8"
                    android:gravity="center"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Title"
                    tools:text="🇳🇱" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/tv_status_detail"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:gravity="center"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Title"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorPrimary"
                    tools:text="Hybrid (Автовыбор)" />
            </LinearLayout>
        </LinearLayout>

        <Space
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/space_24" />

        <!--
          THE SUBSCRIPTION SLOT. The subscription card and the server list, or the
          gate block, never both. HomeFragment crossfades between them in place.
        -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/subscription_slot"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:orientation="vertical">

            <!--
              THE SUBSCRIPTION CARD - a swipeable carousel, one page per subscription,
              carrying that subscription's name, its traffic pill, its last update and
              auto-update interval, the operator's notice, and its own actions:
              refresh, ping, pin, support, Telegram, delete (long press), and the
              chevron that collapses the list below.

              It is a CARD on this screen and not a «Подписка» row that navigates
              away: the owner's screen shows the subscription here, and the actions
              act on the page you are looking at.

              ViewPager2 cannot wrap_content, so HomeFragment measures every page and
              fixes the height to the tallest - one stable height, so peeking
              neighbours stay aligned. Page dots appear only past one subscription.
            -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/group_home_meta"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="vertical">

                <androidx.viewpager2.widget.ViewPager2
                    android:id="@+id/vp_home_meta"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:clipToPadding="false"
                    android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
                    android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter" />

                <LinearLayout
                    android:id="@+id/ll_home_meta_dots"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_gravity="center_horizontal"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
                    android:gravity="center_vertical"
                    android:orientation="horizontal"
                    android:visibility="gone" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!--
              THE SERVER LIST, INLINE, right below the card that owns it.

              This is the ONLY place in the product a server can be picked: the
              owner removed the Серверы destination on 2026-07-26 and none of its
              functions were moved elsewhere, so a Главная without this list would
              leave the app with no server selection at all.

              Tapping a row SELECTS, and never connects; when a tunnel is up the
              shell offers an explicit «применить». That contract lives in
              MainActivity.setSelectServer and is not this screen's to change.

              nestedScrollingEnabled=false: it scrolls with the page, it does not
              scroll inside it. HomeFragment pads its bottom by the shell's
              listBottomInset so the last row clears the overlaid bottom bar.
            -->
            <androidx.recyclerview.widget.RecyclerView
                android:id="@+id/rv_home_servers"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
                android:clipToPadding="false"
                android:nestedScrollingEnabled="false"
                android:scrollbars="none" />

            <!-- Offline: the card and the rows keep their last value and the screen
                 says so, rather than emptying. -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/tv_stale_hint"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
                android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter"
                android:text="@string/home_stale_hint"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Caption"
                android:visibility="gone"
                tools:visibility="visible" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <include
            android:id="@+id/layout_gate"
            layout="@layout/layout_home_empty" />
    </LinearLayout>
</androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView>
